+````markdown name=ops/hsm/hsm_iam_policies.md
+```text
+HSM / KMS IAM policy examples & guidance
+
+1) AWS example - minimal signer role policy (attach to pipeline role that runs cosign)
+{
+  "Version": "2012-10-17",
+  "Statement": [
+    {
+      "Sid": "AllowUseOfAegisCosignKey",
+      "Effect": "Allow",
+      "Action": [
+        "kms:Sign",
+        "kms:GetPublicKey",
+        "kms:DescribeKey"
+      ],
+      "Resource": "arn:aws:kms:us-west-2:123456789012:key/<key-id>"
+    }
+  ]
+}
+
+2) GCP example - IAM binding to allow asymmetric sign:
+gcloud kms keys add-iam-policy-binding aegis-cosign \\
+  --location=global --keyring=aegis-keyring \\
+  --member=serviceAccount:signer@project.iam.gserviceaccount.com \\
+  --role=roles/cloudkms.signerVerifier
+
+3) Azure KeyVault - Access policy (example for a managed identity)
+az keyvault set-policy --name <vault-name> --object-id <principal-id> --key-permissions sign get
+
+Guidance:
+- Limit signer principals to CI/CD signing agents and emergency operator roles.
+- Separate roles: signing vs key management vs key creation/rotation should be distinct.
+- Enforce MFA & strict approval flows for any key rotation or alias change.
+- Record all key admin operations in a separate audit trail (CloudTrail, GCP Audit Logs, Azure Monitor).
